    overview: "The Prophet put his food on the ground, and never ate from a raised table. A cloth on the floor is nearer to humility, and its name reminds the eater of the last journey. Ghazali then weighs four things said to have come in after the Prophet's time: tables, sieves, washing powder and eating one's fill.",
    thesis: "Eating from a cloth on the floor is nearer the Prophet's practice and to humility. But a raised table is not forbidden. Not every new thing is a blameworthy innovation, and the four new things are not equal. The worst of them is eating one's fill.",
